From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:23:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: One walk of the variable store for the
 option lock

With the option lock armed, every SMMSTORE write first reads each
protected option from the variable store as it would be after the write:
one efi_fv_get_option() for bios_lock and one for bootmedia_lock, two
walks of the whole store. The overlay of the write has no mmap, so each
walk reads every header and name and the erased tail through readat
from the memory-mapped flash. On a ThinkCentre M920x a variable write
from the OS takes 6 to 8 SMIs (MSR_SMI_COUNT) and 0.52-0.60 s, about
85 ms an SMI, growing with the store; the flash write itself takes a
few milliseconds.

Add efi_fv_get_options(), which finds several variables of one GUID in
one walk, each as efi_fv_get_option() would find it alone (a match in
transition kept until a later one, the first added one ending its
search), and use it for the check of each write and for the latch at
arm. The decision is the same: an option latched on that would read off
after the write refuses it, a store that cannot be read refuses it, a
missing or unreadable option takes its fallback.

TEST=The unit tests of drivers/efi, with efi_test_get_options: the
values and errors of each query as efi_fv_get_option() gives them,
an option in transition behind an added one, a store that is not one.
On the M920x with v1.6.3-rc4 of ouroBIOS a variable write from the OS
takes 0.29 s, 44 ms an SMI, against 0.58 s and 84 ms with rc3.

Change-Id: I607788b7529b4706154ce11027dd690eaee902c7
